    skos:definition "Pulverised fuel ash (PFA) - A type of artifical deposit. It consists of pulverised (fine grade) ash waste from the burning of coal, usually in coal-fired power stations. It is commonly used as an inert fill material, or for the production of breeze blocks. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/04, appendix 1."@en ;
