    skos:definition "Vitrain - A type of bituminous-coal, classified according to lithotype. It is a black, glassy, vitreous coal. It occurs as thin bands, commonly less than 6 or 8 mm in thickness. It is usually very closely jointed and breaks into cubic pieces generally with a conchoidal fracture. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 6.1 and fig. 10."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll> ;
