    owl:sameAs <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/KMB> ;
    skos:broader rockclassall:ECR ;
    skos:definition "Kimberlite - A type of exotic crystalline igneous rock. Kimberlites are currently divided into two groups. Group-1-kimberlite corresponds to archetypal rocks from Kimberley, South Africa that formerly were termed basaltic kimberlites. Group-2-kimberlite corresponds to micaceous or lamprophyric kimberlites. Recent studies have demonstrated that these two groups are mineralogically different and petrogenetically separate rock types. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 6.4."@en ;
