    skos:definition "Ganister - A type of quartz-arenite. It is a hard, fine-grained, quartz-arenite, cemented with silica and possessing a splintery fracture. Traces of roots may be visible. It is associated with coal seams. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 13.6. See also: seat-earth."@en ;
