    skos:definition "Silicate-mudstone - A type of siliciclastic argillaceous rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, all siliciclastic argillaceous rocks are given this group name. They may be further classified as silicate-siltstone or silicate-claystone based on the proportion of silt to clay. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 2.3 and fig. 5."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll> ;
    skos:narrower
        rockclassall:DSMDST ,
        rockclassall:FSIMST ,
        rockclassall:FSLMST ,
