    skos:broader rockclassall:UMR ;
    skos:definition "Pyroxenite - A type of ultramafic-rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is a coarse-grained ultramafic rock with less than 40% olivine, and pyroxene dominant over hornblende. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1 and figs. 9, 15, 16."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll> ;
    skos:narrower
