    skos:broader rockclassall:NCR ;
    skos:definition "Fine-grained normal crystalline rock - In the Rock Classification Scheme, a crystalline rock is fine-grained if its average crystal size is less than 0.25 mm. This classification is used for fine-grained, very fine-grained, and glassy crystalline igneous rocks. The class includes felsite, mafite, glassy-igneous-rock, and porphyry. This group corresponds to the volcanic division of the IUGS scheme. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 1.3 and figs. 1, 3."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll> ;
    skos:narrower
