    skos:broader rockclassall:PS_SSR ;
    skos:definition "Seat-earth - A term for a bed of rock underlying a coal seam. It represents the soil that supported the vegetation from which the coal was formed. A highly siliceous seat earth is known as a ganister. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 13.6."@en ;
