    skos:definition "Phosphorite - In the Rock Classification Scheme, all lithified phosphate-rich sedimentary rocks are given this group name. This is the lithified equivalent of phosphate-sediment. The textural classification of phosphorites follows that for limestone. The classification of phosphorites composed dominantly of one constituent similarly follows that for limestone. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 4.2 and fig. 8."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll> ;
    skos:narrower
