    skos:definition "Basalt - A type of basaltic-rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, this name is used for a fine-grained crystalline igneous rock when the modal mineralogy is available, and the mineral mode plots in fields 9 and 10 of the quartz - alkali feldspar - plagioclase - feldspathoid (QAPF) diagram. Andesite and basalt may be separated chemically using SiO<sub>2</sub> content: if wt% SiO<sub>2</sub> is less than 52% the rock is basalt. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.2 and figs. 17a, 19."@en ;
